{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יכופר", :translit "yechupar", :gloss "it is atoned / it will be expiated"} {:he "אם יכופר העון", :translit "im yechupar ha-avon", :gloss "if the iniquity is atoned"} {:he "בזאת יכופר עון יעקב", :translit "bazot yechupar avon ya'akov", :gloss "by this is atoned the iniquity of Jacob"} {:he "בחסד ואמת יכופר עון", :translit "b'chesed v'emet yechupar avon", :gloss "through kindness and truth iniquity is atoned"} {:he "אם יכופר העון עד תמותון", :translit "im yechupar ha-avon ad tamutun", :gloss "if the iniquity is atoned until you die"} {:he "בחסד", :translit "b'chesed", :gloss "through kindness"} {:he "גמילות חסדים", :translit "gemilut chasadim", :gloss "acts of kindness"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["יכופר" "אם יכופר העון" "בזאת יכופר עון יעקב" "בחסד ואמת יכופר עון"]} {:kind :other, :note "Verse chain: Isaiah 27:9 quoted with its word 'בזאת' linking to the other three יכופר verses"} {:kind :other, :note "Rabba bar Rav Huna lived sixty years as divine measure-for-measure reward for acts of kindness"}], :frame {:text "The word יכופר appears four times in Scripture, listed by Ba'al HaTurim here. He builds a conceptual chain around the three other occurrences. Isaiah 22:14 states אם יכופר העון עד תמותון, which Yoma 86b interprets to mean that repentance and Yom Kippur suspend punishment but death fully scourges it away. Isaiah 27:9 then says בזאת יכופר עון יעקב, raising the question: by what means? Proverbs 16:6 answers בחסד ואמת יכופר עון. Rabba bar Rav Huna, who was devoted to גמילות חסדים, lived exactly sixty years (Shabbat 118a; see also Mo'ed Katan 28a where his lifespan is discussed). His example illustrates that acts of kindness are a vehicle for atonement.", :sources ["Isaiah 22:14" "Isaiah 27:9" "Proverbs 16:6" "Yoma 86b" "Shabbat 118a" "Mo'ed Katan 28a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["יכופר" "אם יכופר העון" "בזאת יכופר עון יעקב" "בחסד ואמת יכופר עון"], :